  "body": "## What changed (#738, maintainer-reported, P1)\n\n1. **Moves compose on the current pose.** Laying on a face or on three points now computes the lay in the setup's current alignment and composes it onto that alignment, through new `pick::lay_on_plane_in` / `lay_on_points_in` and `setup_turn::held_centre`. Before, each move went back to the import pose first. Axes already composed. Each move is still one `AlignPartToSetup`, and one undo returns to the previous pose exactly. Re-applying the same pick is a zero step and is refused as \"already holds the part that way\".\n2. **One flow.** The top row now reads \"Part alignment - each move starts from where the part sits now\", and its tooltip describes the flow.\n   - \"Start from a preset\" presets turn the part from where it sits, and so does the typed \"Turn by\", through the new `CommandKind::TurnPart` → `AlignPartToSetup::turn_by`.\n   - \"As modelled\" is the one reset.\n   - The pickers' Apply tooltips say a move starts from the current pose and is one undo step.\n3. **Readable status.** It now reads \"1 face selected\", \"2 points selected\" or \"1 edge selected\" (`pick_words`).\n   - Points show where they are: \"Point 2: on 'part' (x, y, z) mm\".\n   - Internal ids (\"Face 0xccc7c…\") never show; app refusals on the page are stripped of \" 0x…\".\n4. **Picks you can see.** `align_pick_viz::paint`:\n   - picked faces are filled with the pick violet (alpha 96);\n   - picked points are 6 px filled discs;\n   - picked edges are 4 px strokes.\n\n**Splits, so no large file grows:**\n- `commands/align_stock.rs` comes out of `setup_align.rs` (422 → 298 lines).\n- `state_align.rs` comes out of `state.rs` (4116 → 4062 lines).\n- No snapshot PNG changed.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/738-align-flow.md`.\n\n## Pinned by\n- `align_compose` (new, 3 tests):\n  - axes then face;\n  - face then three points;\n  - turn-by after a lay, for both pivots, plus the zero and NaN refusals.\n\n  Each checks that the second move composes on the first, and that undo, undo and redo step back exactly.\n- `setup_align_tests::a_preset_after_a_face_lay_composes_and_as_modelled_is_the_one_reset` (real clicks, Ctrl+Z).\n- `setup_plane_tests::the_pick_status_counts_the_face_and_never_shows_an_id` and `setup_points_tests::the_pick_status_counts_the_points_and_never_shows_an_id`.\n- `plane_face_pick::picked_faces_fill_points_are_discs_and_edges_are_bold` (paint assertions on the rendered shell).\n- `pick_words` unit tests.\n\n## Tested\n- **app suites:** all green. lib 107, `align_compose` 3, `plane_align` 9, `plane_align_edges` 5, `points_align` 8, `axis_align` 10, `setup_align` 9, `turn_pivot` 5, `commands_undo` 32, `project_roundtrip` 71, `wcs_align` 5, `mcp_setup` 6, `fixture_locate` 11, `winding_align` 9, `setup_carry` 9, `setup_relative` 9, `setup_stock_source` 6, `fixture_locate_stock` 3, `wcs_view_pose` 3.\n- **ui suites:** all green, lib 447.\n- **clippy `-D warnings`:** ui lib+tests and the app lib are clean.\n\n## Not exercised / for the hand check\n- The look of the fill, discs and bold edges on a real part, including a tilted face.\n- How the new wording reads in the narrow properties pane.\n- Pressing \"Turn by\" Apply twice turns the part twice; this is intended.\n- **Behaviour change:** MCP `lay_part_on_points` / `lay_part_on_plane` now also compose, since they share the command.\n\n**Stays a draft until the maintainer or user hand-checks it** (binary: `~/camcraft-builds/camcraft-ui-738`).\n\nChangelog: Setup page alignment: face, three-point, axis and preset moves now apply to the part where it sits (one undo step each); pick status reads \"N face(s)/point(s)/edge(s) selected\"; picked faces are filled, points are discs and edges bold (#738)\n\nFixes #738\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
